"""
Colour stops for the additional thermal palettes (BGR, cold -> hot).

Generated by sampling well-known colormaps; only the sampled numbers are embedded, so nothing
here needs those packages at runtime. Sources and licences:
  - matplotlib colormaps (matplotlib licence, PSF-based) and ColorBrewer sets (Apache 2.0, C. Brewer)
  - colorcet (P. Kovesi, CC BY 4.0) - https://colorcet.holoviz.org
  - Scientific colour maps (F. Crameri, MIT) - https://www.fabiocrameri.ch/colourmaps/
  - seaborn palettes (BSD-3-Clause)
  - rain, cyan_hot, blue_hot, banded_* are hand-defined approximations, not vendor LUTs.

"gradient" entries are interpolated across the 256-entry LUT; "steps" entries are
flat bands (one colour per band) for high-contrast banded palettes.
"""

